	<Notes>
		GENERAL
-------------
Q: Why Blood Mage and Chaos Conversion?
A: Blood Mage homogenizes different damage types when using different elemental skills, and provides 15% base Critical Hit Chance. This combination allows us to reliably scale any combination of Elemental skills.

Q: Why not run unconverted Frostbolt (pure Cold)?
A: Because it&apos;s more expensive (due to Rakiata&apos;s Flow), whilst the Chaos version has higher damage potential. However, it does require you to apply Wither stacks and manually upkeep Despair. The Cold variant is mechanically less involved.

Q: Why Frostbolt and not Fireball?
A: Frostbolt doesn&apos;t need Infusions, and potentially shotguns single targets much harder.

SKILLS
---------
Ember Fusillade:
 - One-click wonder with Unleash to increase clear speed and single target damage.
 - Because of Unleash, the downsides of Considered Casting and Deliberation are negligible.
 - The damage reduction from Unleash does not seem to affect the Embers.

Frostbolt:
 - Bread and butter for clearing.
 - Snakepit makes Frostbolt explode on impact with monsters and Frost Wall instead of it piercing.
 - Keep spamming this to stack Life Regeneration from Sacrifice of Blood.

Frost Wall:
 - As mentioned above, allows you to shotgun single targets with the overlapping explosions.
 - Shotgunning does require a good placement of the Frost Walls and timing it with incoming Frostbolt projectiles, or hugging the target entirely, so keep that in mind.

Chaos Bolt:
 - Another one-click wonder with Unleash to apply full Wither stacks per cast.

Despair:
 - More damage. Duh.

GEAR
--------
Rathpith Globe:
 - Despite the nerfs, still the biggest source of damage for a Crit build like this.

Veil of the Night + Kaom&apos;s Heart:
 - Biggest sources of Life, and therefore damage through Gore Spike.
 - No Spirit means no Cast on Critical setup, nor other supportive spells.
 - No Resistances is playable, but makes Waystones with Elemental modifiers dangerous to run, causing more bricks.

Original Sin:
 - Source of Chaos Conversion.

Snakepit:
 - Makes Frostbolt explode, increasing upfront damage and it allows shotgunning with Frost Wall.

Undying Hate (Tecrod):
 - Source of Sacrifice of Blood Keystone for Life Regeneration stacking.
 - Mandatory to sustain Rathpith Globe and utilize Atalui&apos;s Bloodletting.
 - If lucky, can offer Increased Life Recovery Rate on a Notable.

Controlled Metamorphosis:
 - Allows us to efficiently grab Wither Away + Pure Chaos.
 - Also allows us to grab Ice Walls for Frost Wall.
 - Grab Ether Flow for some MS QoL.
 - Easy access to Eldritch Battery for some more Mana to utilize with the Lucidity cluster.

Time-Lost Ruby:
 - These amplify your Life Regeneration and Recovery Rate, boosting Sacrifice of Blood substantially.
	</Notes>
